The note's own history is misleading and it should say so. Its first draft was
swept into 518b10d2b2 (a conductor git add -A commit about a blinded row
audit); its corrected text was swept into df85981bd7 (another agent's commit
about KAN receipts), taken from the shared index. Neither message mentions the
note, so git log cannot lead a reader to it.

Adds a provenance section naming both commits. No analysis changed.

